s very well\", \"solves problems extremely well\", \"takes responsibility seriously\", \"know-it-all\", \"hot temper\".\n\nWe need to decide our vote. Could we still vote for C but note concerns? Or we could shift to B or D. Let's think: The panel hasn't discussed A, B, D yet. We could bring up concerns about C's communication and egocentric attitude, which may affect crew cooperation, a key criterion. Meanwhile B handles stress well and is conscientious, but makes nasty remarks, which also affects crew cooperation. D has hot temper and know-it-all, also problematic. A is a show-off and not open to new ideas, also problematic. So C still seems strongest despite communication issues. So we could support C but ask for more info on crew cooperation for others.\n\nThus our contribution: \"I agree with Sarah that Candidate C's reliability and decision speed are strong, but I am concerned about communication difficulty and egocentric attitude, which could undermine crew cooperation. However, compared to other candidates, their issues are less severe. Therefore I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate C.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: \"makes correct decisions quickly\", \"100% reliable\", \"creates positive atmosphere with crew\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\". Also maybe mention that B makes nasty remarks, which is a bigger issue.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
